  "dom_id": "step-q110269",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Evaluate the geometric series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{6}2(5)^{n-1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the given series is in the form ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},$ it is a geometric series. \n\nTo determine the sum, we use the formula for the sum ${S}_{N}$ of a geometric series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=2,$ $r=5$ and $N=6.$ If we substitute these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{6}2(5)^{n-1} & =2\\cdot \\frac{(1-{5}^{6})}{1-5} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{(1-{5}^{6})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-15\\,624) \\\\  & =7\\,812\\end{aligned}\n$$",
